description: How to write any text a person reads in Ecclesia (UI copy, notifications, seed content, docs)
globs: crates/app/src/views/**,crates/domain/**,crates/app/src/http/**,crates/sdk/src/db/seed*.rs,docs/**,README.md,crates/app/static/**/*.js
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow `docs/PROSE.md` before writing or changing any user-facing text.

Short version:

- Headings name what is on the page. Buttons name the action and its object.
- One idea per sentence. Plain words. Contractions are fine.
- Errors: what happened, then the next step. No blame, no apology.
- Flashes are one to four words.
- Never explain what something *isn't*. Never moralize or reassure.
- Never use household / table / seat / door / hands / valley as nouns. Say church, member, pastor, need, offer, gift.
- No `just`, `simply`, `actually`, `please`, `in order to`, `Oops`, `seamless`, `empower`.
- Placeholders are example values, not instructions.
- Seed content sounds like the person typing into the form.

`us_prose_01` in `crates/app/src/style.rs` enforces the word list. Run `cargo test style` after changing copy.
